   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 782 of the laws of 2021 establishing a construction\nindustry advisory council on public contracting reform, in relation to the\ntiming of a report and the effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S6787",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6787-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§9 & 11, Chap 782 of 2021",
    "lawSection": "Committees",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6787\n\nSPONSOR: COMRIE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 782 of the laws of 2021 establishing a\nconstruction industry advisory council on public contracting reform, in\nrelation to the timing of a report and the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this technical bill is to make changes to Chapter 782 of\nthe Laws of 2021 to provide the construction advisory council a full\nyear to issue its findings and recommendations, and to extend the statu-\ntory timeframe of the advisory council.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Sections 9 and 11 of chapter 782 of the laws of 2021, as\namended by chapter 98 of the laws of 2022, are amended to:\n\na. require the advisory council's report no later than 365 days after\nits first public meeting, and\n\nb. extend the statutory authorization of the advisory council from two\nto four years after the original effective date.\n\nSection 2. This act shall take effect immediately.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIn 2021, the legislature passed legislation establishing an advisory\ncouncil on public contracting reform. Unfortunately, the advisory coun-\ncil's report of its findings and recommendations was statutorily due\nDecember 22, 2022, before the council had even been constituted.  In\naddition, the advisory council's statutory authorization, as amended in\n2022, sunsets December 22, 2023.\n\nThis bill would grant the advisory council one year from its first\npublic meeting to issue its report, and extends the advisory council's\nstatutory sunset by an additional two years. In doing so, this bill will\nensure that the temporary advisory council on public contracting reform\nhas a full opportunity to conduct its work.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter 782 of the Laws of 2021\n\nChapter 98 of the Laws of 2022\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
